# The root gives a merge as the actual of a callable formal, and so does
# a method: the same merge, built by the same constructor. take calls its
# formal. five reads other, a field of the unit, 9. The root gives
# merge(five; y: 5): 14. passed, a method, gives the same merge: 14. under
# has other 20 and calls passed: 25. The root gives a merge of the same
# model with another value: 109, and the first again: 14. The root has a
# native body and a walked one; each builds the node. The merge is written
# with the model first and the bound formal is left at its default: a
# bounded case (steps/defects.md, MERGE-KEEPS-MODEL-INTERFACE). Source
# change, 2026-10-04: this fixture was written merge(y: 5; five), the data
# first, and was red at a limit of the root; it is moved to the model
# first, and the method, the free name and the second merge are added
# (steps/defects.md, T7-DATA-FIRST-SHAPE). Entry 7.
int: other 9

fn: five (int: y) int
    return: y + other

fn: bin () int
    return: 0

fn: take (bin: op) int
    return: op()

fn: passed () int
    return: take: merge(five; y: 5)

fn: under () int
    int: other 20
    return: passed()

int: a (take: merge(five; y: 5))
int: b passed()
int: c under()
int: d (take: merge(five; y: 100))
int: e (take: merge(five; y: 5))
int: ok 7
if: a != 14 || b != 14 || c != 25 || d != 109 || e != 14
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
